# Release archives carry the code only: the calculations/ package and the LICENSE.
# GitHub builds a release's "Source code" zip with `git archive`, which honours export-ignore,
# and Zenodo deposits that zip. Docs, Markdown, studies, notebooks, tests and the container stay
# in the repository and in every clone; they are left out of the archive, not out of git.
#
# Everything is ignored first and the code is let back in. The directory line is needed as
# well as the /** line: an ignored directory is skipped whole, whatever its contents say.
* export-ignore
/calculations -export-ignore
/calculations/** -export-ignore
/LICENSE -export-ignore
